## Schema

### Required

- `driver` (String) Identity provider type: azure, google, gitlab, okta, openid, openid-well-known, oauth2, or verge.io. Changing it replaces the auth source. VergeOS does not change the driver of an existing source.
- `name` (String) Display name shown on the login button. Must be unique.

### Optional

- `button_background_color` (String) Login button background color, as a CSS color. Omit to leave the current value unchanged.
- `button_color` (String) Login button text color, as a CSS color. Omit to leave the current value unchanged.
- `button_fa_icon` (String) Login button icon class, for example bi-google. Omit to leave the current value unchanged.
- `client_secret_wo` (String, Sensitive, Write-Only) OAuth client secret sent on create and when `client_secret_wo_version` changes. Not stored. Do not put `client_secret` in `settings`. Requires Terraform 1.11 or OpenTofu 1.11.
- `client_secret_wo_version` (Number) Version of `client_secret_wo`. Increment it to send a new client secret. Terraform stores this number, not the secret. Changing `client_secret_wo` without changing this version does not update the auth source.
- `debug` (Boolean) Enable provider debug logging. VergeOS turns debug off on its own after about an hour, and the next apply turns it back on when this is true. Omit to leave the current value unchanged.
- `icon_color` (String) Login button icon color, as a CSS color. Omit to leave the current value unchanged.
- `menu` (Boolean) Show the source in the login dropdown instead of as a button. Omit to leave the current value unchanged.
- `settings` (String) Driver settings as one JSON object, without `client_secret`. Use `jsonencode`. Omit to leave the stored document unchanged. Terraform stores this document so a change to a tracked key is planned. `client_secret` belongs in `client_secret_wo`. The server-managed `debug` key inside settings is not tracked.

### Read-Only

- `id` (String) Auth source key assigned by VergeOS.

## Import

Import is supported using the auth source key. `settings` and `client_secret_wo_version` are not read from VergeOS. The next plan sends the settings in configuration. The stored client secret is kept unless `client_secret_wo_version` changes.

```shell
terraform import vergeio_auth_source.example <id>
```
